cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use ziv in your work, please cite it as below."
title: "ziv: an OME-Zarr to IIIF Image API 3.0 tile server and static exporter"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Thalhath
    given-names: Nishad
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0001-9845-9714"
    affiliation: "RIKEN Center for Integrative Medical Sciences"
  - family-names: Kasaragod
    given-names: Deepa
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6540-9259"
    affiliation: "Hiroshima University"
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-09-19"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/nishad/ziv"
url: "https://nishad.github.io/ziv-demos/"
abstract: >-
  A single binary that serves an OME-Zarr image as a IIIF Image API 3.0 Level 2 service and
  exports the same image as a static Level 0 tile tree, using the same rendering code. Selection
  across the dimensions of an OME-Zarr array, and across its segmentation masks, is expressed
  inside the IIIF identifier, so unmodified IIIF clients can consume it.
keywords:
  - OME-Zarr
  - OME-NGFF
  - IIIF
  - bioimaging
  - microscopy
